<p><strong>Summary</strong><br>
From our discussion above, an important strategy emerges: between the two s=
ubarrays, <code>[left : mid]</code> and <code>[mid : right]</code>, we can =
use the sorted one to determine where the target is.</p>
<p>Before examining the subarrays, let=E2=80=99s first <strong>compare the =
target with the value at the midpoint</strong>. If they match, we've found =
our target at <code>mid</code>. If not, then we decide where to adjust our =
search depending on which subarray is sorted, as detailed in the following =
two test cases:</p>
<p><strong>Case 1: the left subarray, <code>[left : mid]</code>, is sorted<=
/strong></p>
<ul>
<li>If the target falls in the range of this left subarray, we narrow the s=
earch space toward the left.</li>
<li>Otherwise, we narrow the search space toward the right.</li>
</ul>
